- 2026-07-21: Dashboard Phase 7a (PLAN 7.1/7.2) done on `feat/dashboard-7a`, all 4 tasks reviewed individually, this completes the first half of Phase 7. First frontend work in this project - a Vite+React+TS+Tailwind app at `dashboard/`, verified differently than every backend phase: `docs/design.md`'s own CI bar for the dashboard is "typecheck+build," not "test," so per-task gates were typecheck+build+targeted-vitest (only the two pieces with real logic - the API client's 401-refresh-retry-once, the polling hook's timer/cleanup - got unit tests; no component snapshot tests). Built: login (raw tenant-ID UUID field, no self-serve registration - nothing in this codebase provisions tenants yet), refresh_token in localStorage / access_token in memory only, a typed API client with exactly-one-refresh-retry on 401, and a live map (Leaflet + react-leaflet) polling `GET /api/v1/pings/latest` every 20s with markers resolved to rep emails via `GET /api/v1/users`. Per-task review caught real gaps: a newer `npm create vite` template auto-generated a live, wired oxlint setup that violated the plan's explicit no-second-linting-tool constraint (removed); four justified deviations in the map task for genuine compiler/library-interop reasons (erasableSyntaxOnly rejecting a parameter-property constructor, jsdom needed for `renderHook`, a `@testing-library/react` fake-timer/jest-global interop gap the reviewer physically reproduced by removing the shim and watching the test hang, a `tsc -b`-only typecheck failure the bare `tsc --noEmit` command couldn't see). That last thread continued into the final whole-branch review, which proved the bare `npx tsc --noEmit` gate every task had been self-verifying against was a complete no-op (root tsconfig is solution-style, checks zero files) by injecting a real type error and watching it pass silently - fixed with a `tsc -b`-backed `typecheck` script, plus enabling `strict: true` in `tsconfig.app.json` (the plan called for strict mode; the newer